:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=VRYCFG.Vary Configuration (VRYCFG)
:P.Use the Vary Configuration (VRYCFG) command to vary configuration
objects on or off.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/CFGOBJ'.Configuration object (CFGOBJ)
:P.The configuration object&colon. a line, controller or device
description, or a network server or interface description.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 256 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 11 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *APPN, *PRVCFGTYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/CFGTYPE'.Type (CFGTYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NWS, *LIN, *CTL, *MLBRSC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/STATUS'.Status (STATUS)
:P.The status for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ON:EPK.
:PD.On.
:PT.:PK.*OFF:EPK.
:PD.Off.
:PT.:PK.*UNPROTECTED:EPK.
:PD.Not protected.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RESET, *ALLOCATE, *DEALLOCATE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/RANGE'.Range (RANGE)
:P.The range for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NET, *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/VRYWAIT'.Vary on wait (VRYWAIT)
:P.The vary on wait for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 15 to 180.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CFGOBJ, *NOWAIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/ASCVRYOFF'.Asynchronous vary off (ASCVRYOFF)
:P.Whether to asynchronous vary off.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/RESET'.Reset (RESET)
:P.Whether to reset.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/RSRCNAME'.Resource name (RSRCNAME)
:P.The hardware resource name, as WRKHDWRSC shows it.
:P.Up to 16 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/FRCVRYOFF'.Forced vary off (FRCVRYOFF)
:P.The forced vary off for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LOCK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/SBMMLTJOB'.Submit multiple jobs (SBMMLTJOB)
:P.Whether to submit multiple jobs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QBATCH is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/GENPTHCERT'.Generate path certificate (GENPTHCERT)
:P.Whether to generate path certificate.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VRYCFG/RESETSYS'.Reset system (RESETSYS)
:P.Whether to reset system.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKCFGSTS.Work with Configuration Status (WRKCFGSTS)
:P.Use the Work with Configuration Status (WRKCFGSTS) command to show
the status of configuration objects and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCFGSTS/CFGTYPE'.Type (CFGTYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NWS, *NWI, *LIN, *CTL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCFGSTS/CFGD'.Configuration description (CFGD)
:P.The configuration description for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CMN, *ASYNC, *BSC, *DDI, *ELAN, *FAX, *FR,
*IDLC, *NET, *PPP, *SDLC, *TDLC, *TRLAN, *WLS, *X25, *APPC, *DSP, *PRT,
*VWS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCFGSTS/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCFGSTS/RMTLOCNAME'.Remote location (RMTLOCNAME)
:P.The remote location name of the system at the other end of the
connection.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCFGSTS/ASTLVL'.Assistance level (ASTLVL)
:P.The assistance level the user's displays show&colon. basic
(Operational Assistant), intermediate (the system displays) or advanced.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*INTERMED:EPK.
:PD.Intermediate assistance&colon. the system displays.
:PT.:PK.*ADVANCED:EPK.
:PD.Advanced assistance&colon. the system displays with more on each and
fewer keys shown.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCFGSTS/RANGE'.Range (RANGE)
:P.The range for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NET, *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCFGSTS/STATUS'.Status (STATUS)
:P.The status for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ACTIVE:EPK.
:PD.Active.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FAILED, *VARYOFF, *VARYON, *AVAILABLE.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
